# Quick Start Guide

Get your database up and running in 5 minutes!

## Prerequisites

- ✅ PostgreSQL installed and running
- ✅ Node.js 18+ installed
- ✅ Project dependencies installed (`npm install`)

## 🚀 Setup Steps

### 1. Configure Environment

```bash
# Copy environment template
cp .env.example .env

# Edit .env and update DATABASE_URL
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://username:password@localhost:5432/{{projectName}}_dev"
```

### 2. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install @prisma/client prisma bcryptjs
npm install -D tsx @types/bcryptjs
```

### 3. Initialize Database

```bash
# Generate Prisma Client
npm run db:generate

# Push schema to database (for development)
npm run db:push

# OR create a migration (recommended)
npm run db:migrate
```

### 4. Seed Demo Data

```bash
npm run db:seed
```

### 5. Verify Setup

```bash
# Open Prisma Studio to browse your database
npm run db:studio
```

## 🎉 Done!

Your database is ready! You now have:

- ✅ User authentication tables
- ✅ Subscription management
- ✅ Payment tracking
- ✅ Demo accounts (see below)

